# Supabase
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key

# Confirmation-email links point here.
#
# You normally do NOT need to set this. On Vercel the app works out its own
# address from VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL, falling back to VERCEL_URL, so
# a fresh deployment sends working links with zero configuration.
#
# Set it only when the automatic answer is wrong:
#   - you serve the app on your own domain, e.g. https://lunch.example.com
#     -- then this is the key that overrides it, and it wins over both Vercel
#        variables. Set it for Production, Preview and Development alike.
#   - you host somewhere other than Vercel, where neither Vercel variable
#     exists at all.
#
# Anything with a path or query is reduced to its origin. A bare host with no
# scheme also works. Local development uses http://localhost:3000.
#
# Supabase builds confirmation-email links from the project's Site URL
# setting (Authentication -> URL Configuration) only when the app supplies no
# address of its own. If you override this, change it there too -- the two
# drifting apart is the failure these notes exist to prevent:
#   - Site URL
#   - the redirect allow-list, which must admit the same origin
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://lunch.example.com

# Google Gemini (used by Vercel AI SDK)
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=your_google_api_key

# Optional: enable the read-only Sofa import preview for a reviewed Restaurant
# UUID in THIS environment. The source URL is fixed on the server; its exact
# branch name/address are rechecked before fetching. Do not copy IDs between
# databases. The preview requires an Admin and does not publish offers.
# SOFA_IMPORT_RESTAURANT_ID=your_reviewed_restaurant_uuid
# SUSHI_IMPORT_RESTAURANT_ID=your_reviewed_sushi_friends_restaurant_uuid
# Optional exact reviewed address when the stored spelling differs from the default.
# SUSHI_IMPORT_BRANCH_ADDRESS=ul. Marco Polo 9e, Wrocław
# Optional stage-2 publication: a server-only random secret of at least 32 characters.
# Generate independently per environment; never expose it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Without it, imports remain previews only. Requires the stage-2 SQL migration.
# LUNCH_IMPORT_SIGNING_SECRET=your_random_server_only_secret

# Optional. Overrides the pinned model in src/lib/ai/models.ts. For
# experimentation only; the app needs no value here.
# AI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Playwright suites that touch a real Supabase. Leave unset to skip them.
#
# __tests__/e2e/post-auth-migration.spec.ts seeds and cleans up through the
# service-role key, so point these at a DISPOSABLE project -- never at one
# holding real data. It deletes what it matches by token prefix.
#
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_TEST_ENABLED=true
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_TEST_URL=https://your-disposable-project.supabase.co
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_TEST_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your_disposable_service_role_key
#
# The migration-failure suite additionally needs the trigger from
# supabase/tests/fixtures/playwright-migration-failure.sql applied BY HAND to
# that disposable project, then this variable set to `installed` to confirm it.
# Nothing applies it automatically -- a test cannot honestly assert that its own
# sabotage is in place.
#
# PLAYWRIGHT_SUPABASE_TEST_MIGRATION_FAILURE_FIXTURE=installed
